dynare-rust
===========

dynare-rust is an unofficial Rust port of Dynare 7.2 (https://www.dynare.org).
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Dynare Team.

Dynare is Copyright (C) 1996-2026 Dynare Team and is distributed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version.
The Dynare Team's members and former members are listed in Dynare's
license.txt.

Most algorithms in this repository were translated from Dynare's MATLAB
sources (the `matlab/` tree of Dynare 7.2) and its C++ components (notably the
preprocessor's DataTree and model transformations), and checked against
Dynare's output. This port is therefore a derivative work of Dynare and is
distributed under the same license, GPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE for the full
text.

Reference data
--------------
The JSON, MAT, CSV and log files under reference/ were produced by running
Dynare (7.1 and 7.2, under MATLAB R2025b) on the .mod files next to them, with
the dump scripts in the same folders. They are test fixtures, not part of
Dynare itself.

Third-party content under reference/
------------------------------------
- reference/examples72/: example models shipped with Dynare 7.2
  (`examples/` of the Dynare distribution), Copyright Dynare Team,
  GPL-3.0-or-later, some lightly edited for the tests (headers kept).
- reference/examples72/schorfheide_2000/schorfheide_2000_data.m and
  reference/misc/schorfheide_2000_data.m: data of Schorfheide (2000),
  "Loss function-based evaluation of DSGE models", Journal of Applied
  Econometrics. Copyright 2000-2022 Frank Schorfheide, 2023 Dynare Team,
  licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode),
  as distributed with Dynare.
- Other .mod files under reference/ are test models written for this project
  or adapted from Dynare's examples and test suite (GPL-3.0-or-later).
